        <h2 id="timings" class="scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
          1. Dry Times by Type and Depth
        </h2>

        <p>
          Spackle dries by evaporation, so the depth of the fill matters more than anything printed on the container. A skim across a dent loses its water in minutes; a plug half an inch deep has to lose it through a surface that is already drying and closing up.
        </p>

